oduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:4420fb212ae7ff38aec3b98a7653c962feeec778d55e82e8365b0d9c6ddea74e","file":"preprints/An-atomic-certificate-for-triangular-lattice-universal-optimality-September-26-2026/build/main.tex","line":95,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"a637b73fba30a36abc66b844a8f6d6b5e334423433df887f81b3ab097047f1e0","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/An-atomic-certificate-for-triangular-lattice-universal-optimality-September-26-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:4420fb212ae7ff38aec3b98a7653c962feeec778d55e82e8365b0d9c6ddea74e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/An-atomic-certificate-for-triangular-lattice-universal-optimality-September-26-2026/build/main.tex#L95"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:gaussian}\nFor every $\\alpha>0$ there is a real radial Schwartz function\n$f_\\alpha:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R$ such that\n\\[\n f_\\alpha(x)\\le k_\\alpha(x),\\qquad\n \\widehat f_\\alpha(\\xi)\\ge0\n \\quad(x,\\xi\\in\\mathbb R^2),\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n f_\\alpha(a)=k_\\alpha(a)\\quad(a\\in A\\setminus\\{0\\}),\\qquad\n \\widehat f_\\alpha(w)=0\\quad(w\\in A^*\\setminus\\{0\\}).\n\\]\nFor $\\alpha\\ge1$, the construction uses two finite $20$-by-$20$ interpolation\nblocks and an absolutely summable infinite correction."}
